                <pb facs="0943" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672(1929)/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Angora</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-08T18:00:00+02:00">September 8, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 8—5:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. I have begun negotiations for Treaty of Commerce and Navigation and shall
                    postpone leave of absence until they are completed. Expect to cable Turkish
                    counter proposals within a day or two. The proposed Turkish alterations in
                    Department’s text appear to be chiefly clarifications and precisions rather than
                    matters of principle.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
